{#- The architecture drawing, shared by /docs/ in the app and /code/ on the public site.

    One copy, because two copies of a diagram is two diagrams that disagree about the system a
    few months from now. It is inline SVG rather than a rendering library: the app's CSP allows
    scripts from 'self' and gstatic only, so a diagram from a CDN could not run, and a hundred
    kilobytes of renderer to draw a dozen boxes would be the wrong trade if it could.

    The lanes group by what a thing is FOR rather than by which file it lives in, which is the
    question somebody looking at an architecture picture is actually asking. -#}
      <svg viewBox="0 0 700 518" class="w-full min-w-[560px]" role="img"
        aria-label="Four layers. You, in a browser. Two static sites that hold no secrets. One API that verifies the token, re-reads the role and holds every key. Below it Firebase for identity, Postgres for messages, checks and saved answers, and twenty-four upstream services, six of which need a credential. The app’s map tiles are the one thing the browser fetches itself.">
        <defs>
          <marker id="flow-arrow" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto">
            <path d="M0,0 L8,4 L0,8 z" class="dg-arrow"/>
          </marker>
        </defs>

        {# Lanes first, so every box sits on top of its band. #}
        <g>
          <rect x="6" y="6" width="688" height="70" rx="10" class="dg-lane"/>
          <text x="18" y="24" class="dg-lane-label">In your hands</text>

          <rect x="6" y="92" width="688" height="92" rx="10" class="dg-lane"/>
          <text x="18" y="110" class="dg-lane-label">Served as files · no secret is in them</text>

          <rect x="6" y="200" width="688" height="100" rx="10" class="dg-lane"/>
          <text x="18" y="218" class="dg-lane-label">The only thing that decides</text>

          <rect x="6" y="316" width="688" height="196" rx="10" class="dg-lane"/>
          <text x="18" y="334" class="dg-lane-label">What it asks, on your behalf</text>

          {# A band inside the band: everything in it is one of the twenty-four. #}
          <rect x="22" y="342" width="436" height="158" rx="8" class="dg-lane"/>
        </g>

        {# Box to box, so each arrow says which two things talk. Straight, and clear of the lane labels. #}
        <g class="dg-line" marker-end="url(#flow-arrow)">
          <path d="M310,66 L310,120"/>
          <path d="M390,66 L390,120"/>
          <path d="M218,170 L218,226"/>
          <path d="M482,170 L482,226"/>
          <path d="M240,288 L240,352"/>
          <path d="M520,288 L520,352"/>
          <path d="M628,288 L628,352"/>
        </g>

        <g>
          <rect x="290" y="30" width="120" height="36" rx="8" class="dg-box"/>
          <text x="350" y="53" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-label">Your browser</text>

          <rect x="106" y="120" width="224" height="50" rx="8" class="dg-box"/>
          <text x="218" y="141" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-label">tzortzoglou.eu</text>
          <text x="218" y="157" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">the portfolio · one call: the contact form</text>

          <rect x="370" y="120" width="224" height="50" rx="8" class="dg-box"/>
          <text x="482" y="141" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-label">app.tzortzoglou.eu</text>
          <text x="482" y="157" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">signed in · pages only</text>

          {#- The one accent in the drawing: this box is what the picture is about. -#}
          <rect x="60" y="226" width="580" height="62" rx="8" class="dg-box-accent"/>
          <text x="350" y="247" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-label">api.tzortzoglou.eu</text>
          <text x="350" y="263" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">checks the token · re-reads your role · holds every key</text>
          <text x="350" y="278" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">nothing below this line is reachable without it</text>

          <rect x="32" y="352" width="416" height="42" rx="8" class="dg-box-key"/>
          <text x="240" y="369" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-label">Twenty-four upstreams</text>
          <text x="240" y="384" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">six need a key</text>

          {#- By what each is for. The four boxes add up to the twenty-four: the names printed are
              the ones this drawing has always printed, and Live map is the remainder, so a new
              source there changes the count above and nothing here. -#}
          <rect x="32" y="402" width="416" height="40" rx="8" class="dg-box"/>
          <text x="240" y="418" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-label">Sport and headlines</text>
          <text x="240" y="433" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">Jolpica · ESPN · shl.se · hockeyallsvenskan.se · Expressen · Aftonbladet</text>

          <rect x="32" y="450" width="172" height="40" rx="8" class="dg-box"/>
          <text x="118" y="466" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-label">Weather and travel</text>
          <text x="118" y="481" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">Open-Meteo · Trafiklab ResRobot</text>

          <rect x="212" y="450" width="92" height="40" rx="8" class="dg-box"/>
          <text x="258" y="466" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-label">Deploys</text>
          <text x="258" y="481" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">GitHub Actions</text>

          <rect x="312" y="450" width="136" height="40" rx="8" class="dg-box"/>
          <text x="380" y="466" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-label">Live map</text>
          <text x="380" y="481" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">the rest of the twenty-four</text>

          <rect x="470" y="352" width="100" height="46" rx="8" class="dg-box"/>
          <text x="520" y="371" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-label">Firebase</text>
          <text x="520" y="386" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">who you are</text>

          <rect x="578" y="352" width="100" height="46" rx="8" class="dg-box"/>
          <text x="628" y="371" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-label">Postgres</text>
          <text x="628" y="386" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">messages · caches</text>

          {#- Live state, drawn only where a page loads scripts/arch-live.js (/code/). Hidden until
              a state arrives, so /docs/ in the app and a failed read both show the plain drawing.
              The words for each dot are in the line under the diagram, never colour alone. -#}
          <circle cx="318" cy="132" r="4.5" class="dg-live" data-live="site"/>
          <circle cx="582" cy="132" r="4.5" class="dg-live" data-live="app"/>
          <circle cx="628" cy="238" r="4.5" class="dg-live" data-live="api"/>
          <circle cx="666" cy="364" r="4.5" class="dg-live" data-live="database"/>
          <circle cx="436" cy="364" r="4.5" class="dg-live" data-live="upstreams"/>

          <text x="472" y="424" class="dg-sub">none of these twenty-four is ever</text>
          <text x="472" y="439" class="dg-sub">called from your browser</text>
          {#- The exception, named rather than left off. The app's map tiles are fetched by the
              browser itself, because a tile is asked for one square at a time as you pan and
              standing in front of a few hundred of those would mean running a tile server. It is
              not drawn as a box because it hangs off the browser at the top, not off the API at
              the bottom, and an arrow that long would cross every layer to say one thing. -#}
          <text x="472" y="462" class="dg-sub">the app’s map tiles are the one exception,</text>
          <text x="472" y="477" class="dg-sub">fetched by your browser itself</text>
        </g>
      </svg>
